comments.body:
@seelabs, my unit tests will be a source on on-going irritation for you :smile:.

1. Would it help if I divided the test into two sections?  I'll make a run at separating the gw1 -> alice -> gw2 section from the alice -> gw1 -> bob section.

2. I struggled a lot getting this test to work and to verify that the failures were for the reasons I expected.  When I struggle I'm likely to add more comments.  For example,
```
// Pay alice so there is something to ripple.
env (pay (gw1, alice, USD1 (10)));
```
If the comment only said "pay alice", I'd agree with you.  But it turns out that unless you pay alice first, no rippling will occur.  This may seem obvious to you, but it was not obvious to me
